on for parenthesis splitter operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"\") -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\nclass InvalidParenthesesError(ParenSplitterError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when parentheses are unbalanced or malformed.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, position: int = -1) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.position = position\nclass EmptyInputError(ParenSplitterError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input contains no meaningful parenthesis characters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input contains no parenthesis characters\") -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\nclass InvalidCharacterError(ParenSplitterError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an unsupported character is found in the input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, char: str, position: int) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.char = char\n        self.position = position\nclass ParenthesisGroup:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates a single balanced parenthesis group string.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, group: str) -> None:\n        if not group:\n            raise ValueError(\"group must be non-empty\")\n        self.group: str = group\n    \n    def as_str(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Returns the raw group string.\"\"\"\n        return self.group\ndef normalize_input(input_str: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes all whitespace characters from the input string.\"\"\"\n    return \"\".join(ch for ch in input_str if not ch.isspace())\ndef is_parenthesis_char(ch: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a character is an opening or closing parenthesis.\"\"\"\n    return ch in (\"(\", \")\")\nclass ParenSplitterService:\n    \"\"\"Core parsing and validation logic for splitting parenthesis groups.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._allowed_chars = {\"(\", \")\"}\n\n    def split(self, input_str: str) -> List[ParenthesisGroup]:\n        \"\"\"Parses the input string into a list of ParenthesisGroup objects.\"\"\"\n        s = normalize_input(input_str)\n        if not s:\n            raise EmptyInputError()\n        self._validate_chars(s)\n        raw_groups = self._scan_and_split(s)\n        return [ParenthesisGroup(g) for g in raw_groups]\n\n    def _validate_chars(self, s: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures all characters in the string are valid parentheses.\"\"\"\n        for i, ch in enumerate(s):\n            if not is_parenthesis_char(ch):\n                raise InvalidCharacterError(f\"Invalid char '{ch}' at position {i}\", ch, i)\n\n    def _scan_and_split(self, s: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Scans the string to identify and extract balanced top-level parenthesis groups.\"\"\"\n        groups: List[str] = []\n        buf: List[str] = []\n        depth = 0\n        for i, ch in enumerate(s):\n            if ch == \"(\":\n                depth += 1\n            else:  # ch == \")\"\n                depth -= 1\n                if depth < 0:\n                    raise InvalidParenthesesError(\"Extra closing parenthesis\", position=i)\n            buf.append(ch)\n            if depth == 0 and buf:\n                groups.append(\"\".join(buf))\n                buf.clear()\n        if depth != 0:\n            raise InvalidParenthesesError(\"Unclosed open parenthesis\", position=len(s)-1)\n        return groups\nclass ParenController:\n    \"\"\"Public API adapter, providing a simple interface to the parenthesis splitting service.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: ParenSplitterService = None) -> None:\n        self._service = service or ParenSplitterService()\n\n    def separate_groups(self, input_str: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Splits an input string into separate balanced parenthesis groups.\"\"\"\n        groups = self._service.split(input_str)\n        return [g.as_str() for g in groups]\n_default_controller = ParenController()\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this funct